{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/pulls/20","id":4987930026,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTVt43s8AAAABKU3Fqg","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie/swift-steward/pull/20","diff_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie/swift-steward/pull/20.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie/swift-steward/pull/20.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/issues/20","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/pulls/20/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/pulls/20/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/issues/20/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/swift-steward/statuses/002306a3adfe4f99c7b64a934efd1b77d327da90","number":20,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rename the CLI binary to steward","user":{"login":"marosoaie","id":2098985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTg5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2098985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Step 1.6 of the split plan: the CLI binary becomes `steward` (decision 1). Every subcommand behaves as before; only the name changes. `CommandConfiguration.version` goes to **2.0.0**, the version the maintainer picked for this release. The matching tap PR is [marosoaie/homebrew-tap#2](https://github.com/marosoaie/homebrew-tap/pull/2) (draft until the release exists).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Package:** executable product `steward`. The executable target is `StewardCLI` (was `git-diff-parser`) and the root command type is `StewardCommand` (was `GitDiffParser`). The target isn't called `steward` because a module `steward` would collide with the planned `Steward` library module on case-insensitive file systems (`Modules/steward.swiftmodule` vs `Steward.swiftmodule`). `StewardCommand` can't shadow that module the way a type named `Steward` would.\n- **CLI:** `commandName: \"steward\"`, plus the `changes`/`filter` help examples.\n- **Docs:** the README (title, install, examples, CI recipe, and a note that `brew upgrade` migrates `git-diff-parser` installs), the AGENTS.md title and product table, and the INTERNALS.md intro.\n- **pr.yml:** the self-run calls `.build/debug/steward filter`.\n- **release.yml:** the version check runs `.build/release/steward --version`. The zip is `steward-$VERSION-macos-arm64.zip` and holds `steward`. The formula bump pins `Formula/steward.rb`, commits as `steward $VERSION`, and never touches `Formula/git-diff-parser.rb`. If the tap has no `Formula/steward.rb` yet, it prints a `::warning::` naming the version and commit to pin by hand, then exits 0. That happens exactly once, on the first steward release (see the checklist). Also replaced `ls` in the Xcode pick with `printf`, as pr.yml already does, so actionlint (shellcheck SC2012) passes on the changed workflow.\n- **Version:** `CommandConfiguration.version` 1.0.2 → 2.0.0. AGENTS.md's release procedure bumps it through a PR before the Release workflow runs, and doing it here leaves the release one dispatch away. Being greater than 1.0.2 also lets `brew upgrade` migrate and rebuild existing installs (tested, see below).\n- **Tests:** `CommandLineTool` runs `steward`. The new \"Command name\" suite checks that the built executable is named `steward`, and that the help of the root command, `changes` and `filter` says `USAGE: steward …` and never mentions `git-diff-parser`.\n\n**Kept on purpose:**\n- The library modules `BuildLogKit`, `DiffDiagnostics` and `StreamParsing`, and the test target `SwiftStewardTests`. None of them carries the old name.\n- The fixture cache folder `git-diff-parser-tests` and `GIT_DIFF_PARSER_SKIP_NETWORK_TESTS`. They hold and gate the library's diff fixtures, and the git-diff-parser repo uses the same folder and variable, so both repos share one download. Renaming them would also invalidate CI's fixture caches.\n- The temp-file prefixes the tests write.\n\n## Release checklist (maintainer)\n\nOrder matters: the old formula must never be pinned to a release that only builds `steward`, and `Formula/steward.rb` can't land until a release that builds `steward` exists. v1.0.2's source builds only `git-diff-parser`; I checked that the renamed formula fails at `bin.install` there.\n\n1. **Merge this PR.** It carries the rename and the 2.0.0 bump. Nothing is released yet, so `brew install marosoaie/tap/git-diff-parser` still installs v1.0.2. The one gap: `brew install --HEAD git-diff-parser` fails from here until step 4, because `main` no longer builds `git-diff-parser`. Landing the tap PR first would instead break `steward` outright, so this order is the lesser gap.\n2. **Dispatch the Release workflow** with `2.0.0` on `main`. It tests, checks that `steward --version` prints 2.0.0, publishes `steward-2.0.0-macos-arm64.zip`, and tags `v2.0.0`. Its last step finds no `Formula/steward.rb` in the tap and warns `Formula/steward.rb is not in the tap yet; pin it to v2.0.0 (<sha>) by hand`. The run stays green, and `git-diff-parser` stays on v1.0.2 and keeps working.\n3. **Re-pin the tap PR**, [marosoaie/homebrew-tap#2](https://github.com/marosoaie/homebrew-tap/pull/2) (branch `rename-formula-to-steward`), to `v2.0.0`, with the same `sed` the workflow uses. The SHA is the one in the warning, which is also what `git ls-remote https://github.com/marosoaie/swift-steward.git refs/tags/v2.0.0` prints:\n   ```sh\n   VERSION=2.0.0 SHA=<sha from the warning>\n   sed -E -i '' -e 's|(tag:[[:space:]]*)\"v[^\"]*\"|\\1\"v'\"$VERSION\"'\"|' \\\n     -e 's|(revision:[[:space:]]*)\"[0-9a-f]*\"|\\1\"'\"$SHA\"'\"|' Formula/steward.rb\n   ```\n   Then commit, push, and mark the PR ready for review.\n4. **Merge the tap PR.** `brew install marosoaie/tap/steward` then installs 2.0.0, and `git-diff-parser` resolves to `steward` through `formula_renames.json`. Because 2.0.0 is newer than the installed 1.0.2, `brew update && brew upgrade` migrates existing installs and rebuilds them as `steward` (tested, see below). Until an install is migrated, `brew outdated` prints \"git-diff-parser was renamed to steward and needs to be migrated by running: brew migrate git-diff-parser\"; `brew upgrade` does that migration by itself. Every later release bumps `Formula/steward.rb` on its own.\n5. **Check:** `brew update && brew upgrade && steward --version` prints 2.0.0. On macOS 26, Homebrew 6 builds from source only with the Command Line Tools installed (`xcode-select --install`); Xcode alone is refused.\n\n## Tests run\n\nAll on macOS 26.6.2 (arm64) with Xcode 27.0 (Swift 6.4). The table's first row ran after the 2.0.0 bump (`002306a`). The rows below it ran on `3a7317b`, the rename alone, whose `--version` was still 1.0.2.\n\n| Check | Inputs | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| **After the 2.0.0 bump** (`002306a`) | full suite; `release.yml`'s version-check step; the 61 v1.0.2 comparison cases | `swift test` (network tests on): **48 tests in 12 suites pass**, 27.9 s. `xcodebuild test`: **TEST SUCCEEDED**, 48 in 12, 26.9 s. `swiftlint` prints nothing; 0 compiler warnings. `steward --version` prints `2.0.0`, and the version check passes for 2.0.0 and fails for 1.0.2. Against brew's v1.0.2: **60/61 identical**, the one difference being `--version` (`1.0.2` → `2.0.0`) |\n| `swift build --build-tests` | whole package | 0 warnings; `.build/debug/steward` exists, no `git-diff-parser` product |\n| `swift test` (network tests on) | full suite | **48 tests in 12 suites pass**, 27.4 s (new: the \"Command name\" suite, 2 tests, one of them run for 3 commands) |\n| `xcodebuild test -scheme swift-steward-Package -destination platform=macOS` | full suite | **TEST SUCCEEDED**, 48 tests in 12 suites, 23.5 s; no compiler warnings |\n| `swiftlint lint --quiet` | whole tree | prints nothing |\n| `actionlint` | `pr.yml`, `release.yml` | clean (release.yml had SC2012 before; fixed) |\n| `cmp` against brew's v1.0.2 `git-diff-parser` (release builds) | 61 cases: `changes` json/text/stdin on the kernel 6.6→6.7, redis 7.0→7.2, swift-argument-parser 1.0→1.5 and swift PR #70000 diffs; `filter` on the SAP 1.5.0 xcodebuild/SwiftLint/SwiftFormat logs × generic/own tool × json/github/text, `--fail-on` note/warning/error, `--tolerance`, `--repo-root`, log and diff on stdin; the cli-smoke log on the kernel diff; `--version`; 5 error cases | **61/61 identical**: stdout bytes, exit codes (47×0, 9×1, 5×64), and stderr after replacing the name |\n| `cmp` against `origin/main`'s release build | the 61 above, plus Sonar (`--tool sonar` × 3 formats, `--fail-on`, stdin) and help (`--help`, `-h`, `changes --help`, `filter --help`, `help changes`, `help filter`) | **70/72 identical**. The 2 differences are `filter --help` and `help filter`, where the shorter name lets one example line stop wrapping |\n| Kernel benchmark, `changes` (release, 3 runs) | 70 MB kernel diff | steward 0.25 s / 68 MB peak (json), 0.26 s / 19 MB (text); v1.0.2 on the same machine 0.28–0.29 s / 68 MB, 0.30 s / 19 MB |\n| pr.yml's \"Fail on new warnings\" step, extracted and run | this branch's diff, build log and SwiftLint log | exit 0; with a planted warning on a changed line it annotates and exits 1 |\n| release.yml's version-check, package and bump steps, extracted and run | `.build/release/steward`; scratch bare copies of the tap | `--version` check: 1.0.2 passes, 9.9.9 fails. The zip holds only `steward`, `cmp`-identical to the build, and its `.sha256` checks. Bump: with no key, skips. On the tap's `main` (no `steward.rb`), warns, exits 0, changes nothing. On the rename branch, changes only `tag:`/`revision:` and commits `steward 9.9.9`; a rerun says it's already pinned |\n| Tap formula's install and test blocks, run by hand | fresh clones, `swift build -c release --disable-sandbox`, then the formula's two test commands | v1.0.2 pin: revision matches, then `bin.install` fails (only `git-diff-parser` built). Re-pinned with the checklist's `sed` to a scratch tag `v9.9.9` on this branch: builds, both tests pass |\n| Real Homebrew install and migration (scratch tap `stewardcheck/tap` with the real formula names; swift-steward served from a scratch repo with a tag `v9.9.9` on this branch, pinned with the checklist's `sed`) | 1. Installed the old `git-diff-parser` 1.0.2 from the tap's `main` (built from GitHub in 23 s). 2. Landed this rename plus the `v9.9.9` pin. An unscoped `brew upgrade --dry-run` reports \"Would migrate formula git-diff-parser to steward\" and an upgrade to 9.9.9. 3. `brew upgrade …/git-diff-parser` migrated the keg, built 9.9.9 in 24 s, and linked `/opt/homebrew/bin/steward`. `git-diff-parser` is unlinked, the 1.0.2 keg is cleaned up, and Homebrew keeps `Cellar/` and `opt/` alias links under the old name. 4. `brew test` passes. 5. The brew-built `steward` is `cmp`-identical to the branch build on the kernel diff (json and text), the SAP xcodebuild and SwiftLint logs, and the Sonar report. 6. After an uninstall (which also removed the alias links), a fresh `brew install …/steward` and `brew test` pass, and `brew install …/git-diff-parser` answers \"steward 9.9.9 is already installed\". Afterwards the scratch tap, its trust entries and caches were removed, and the maintainer's `marosoaie/tap/git-diff-parser` 1.0.2 was reinstalled (same kernel output, `cmp`-checked) |\n| `brew style`, `brew audit --strict --online`, `brew audit --tap`, `brew readall`, `brew info …/git-diff-parser` | the tap branch, tapped locally as a scratch tap (since untapped) | all clean; `git-diff-parser` resolves to `steward` (\"Old Names: git-diff-parser\") |\n\n## Review\n\nCodex (`gpt-6.1-sol`), `codex review --base main`: **0 findings**, on `3a7317b` and again on `002306a` with the version bump (\"The rename is consistent across the package, CLI, tests, CI, and release packaging\").\n\nCodex on the tap PR raised 2 findings, both handled through this checklist:\n- The tap formula is still pinned to v1.0.2 → it's a draft until step 4 re-pins it.\n- A rename alone doesn't rebuild migrated kegs → step 2 now requires a version greater than 1.0.2.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-23T19:06:19Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T10:53:41Z","closed_at":"2026-10-24T10:53:41Z","merged_at":"2026-10-24T10:53:41Z","merge_commit_sha":"130b762314ebb150fa2cb6614ddfe1a07787f05f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"marosoaie:claude/step-1-6-steward-rename-2b4dd3","ref":"claude/step-1-6-steward-rename-2b4dd3","repo":{"id":1297840350,"node_id":"R_kgDOTVt43g","name":"swift-steward","full_name":"marosoaie/swift-steward","owner":{"login":"marosoaie","id":2098985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTg5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2098985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"h